{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The process involved a comprehensive check of all draft application materials against the authoritative inventor sources, which are `input/disclosure.md` and the USER-labeled passages in `input/conversation.md`.\n\nFirst, I read and processed all specified input files, including the disclosure, conversation history, drafting brief, and all draft sections from the title to the abstract, as well as the numeral list and all figure briefs.\n\nNext, I performed a detailed source-tracing analysis. I systematically reviewed every limitation in each of the 22 claims (claims 1-22) and successfully traced each one to a supporting statement in the inventor's disclosure. This included independent apparatus claims 1 and 13, and the independent method claim 18, along with all their dependent claims.\n\nI then verified every numbered part in `draft/numerals.md` against the disclosure, confirming that a source basis exists for each element. The use of these numerals in the detailed description (`draft/08-detailed-description.md`) and the figure briefs (`figures/*.md`) was found to be consistent.\n\nThe detailed description and the figure briefs were reviewed to ensure they did not introduce any new technical matter not supported by the inventor's disclosure. The language used, including descriptions of components \"shown schematically,\" was found to be an appropriate depiction convention that did not add unsupported technical substance.\n\nFinally, I conducted an internal consistency check. Terminology was consistent across all documents and aligned with the instructions in `input/brief.md`. Cross-references, such as the section line for FIG. 5, were verified and found to be correct. The entire application was free of any unresolved placeholders, drafting notes, or internal comments.\n\nThe review concluded without identifying any disclosure fidelity issues, internal inconsistencies, or other errors requiring a finding. The draft is fully supported by the provided sources."}
